Beckn Implementation Guide – Unsecured Loans Use Case

Introduction:
This document provides the implementation guideline for integrating unsecured loans purchase flow over the Beckn-enabled UKI Network. It defines the messaging flows, payload specifications, taxonomy usage, and other supporting configurations to enable seamless interoperability between Beckn Network Participants (BAPs and BPPs). It assumes the reader has a good overview of the Beckn network, its APIs, the overall structure of the schema etc.

Structure of the document:
Outcome Visualization - This is a pictorial or descriptive representation of the different use cases that are supported by the network.
Flow diagrams - This section provides a pictorial representation of the message flows that happen during the use case.
API Calls and Schema - This section provides details on the API calls and the schema of the message that is sent in the form of sample schemas.
Taxonomy and layer 2 configuration - This section provides details on the taxonomy, enumerations and any rules defined for either the use case or by the network.
Notes on writing/integrating with your own software - This section describes ways in which you can integrate (Becknify) your new or existing software
Links to downloadable resources - This section contains the downloadable files referenced in this document.
Sandbox Details - Sandbox links to BAP, Registry/Gateway and BPP.

Outcome Visualization:
Context
Raju is a smallholder farmer from Nashik, Maharashtra. He wants an unsecured loan to buy seeds and fertilizers for the new season. With no access to reliable credit advisory, Raju opens a Beckn-enabled BAP app connected to UKI Network to find and apply for credit from lenders who serve rural/agri-individuals.
Discovery
Raju logs into the UKI-enabled Beckn BAP (Generic Consumer app).
He searches for “Agriculture Inputs Loans” in the BAP application.
BAP shows him a wide range of loan solutions provided by various lenders.
Raju filters the loans:
Entity Type:  Individual Farmer (Other options: Agri Startups, Agri Enterprises, FPO)
Loan Type: Input / Output / Infrastructure
Loan Amount & Tenure
Special Tags: Women-led, MSME, SFAC Certified
Example Results:
Agri Input Boost Loan – ₹50K–₹1L @ 9% | Grameen Fintech | No Collateral | 3-day TAT | Rating: 4.4
Kisan Pragati Credit – ₹30K–₹80K @ 8.5% | Bharat Bank | Optional Video KYC | 5-day TAT | Rating: 4.6
Order
Raju selects the “Agri Input Boost Loan” from various loan options with minimal documentation.
Raju receives more details about the selected loan from the BAP:
Terms & conditions
Processing charges
Estimated EMI structure
Raju is confident about the loan and proceeds to apply.
Raju starts filing the application with the following data:
Name, Aadhaar, PAN
Crop details (optional)
Loan amount
Bank details
Purpose
OTP verification
Raju submits the form after verifying the details. 
He receives a Loan Application ID generated by the lender upon submission.
Fulfilment
After the submission, Raju can log into the consumer app and track his form status using the Loan Application ID.
CIBIL check is done via PAN.
Verification can fail if the Raju’s CIBIL score does not match the requirement.
After successful verification, Raju has to upload a few more documents. [If needed only]
KYC is done through:
Offline Verification
eAadhaar, or
Video KYC (if required by lender)
Once verified:
Raju receives:
Final Loan Quote
Sanction Letter
Raju accepts via OTP or eSign.
Loan is transferred to Raju’s account.
Consumer app confirms transaction and EMI schedule.
Post-Fulfilment
Raju submits a rating for the product that he has purchased. The seller receives the rating and can request for further feedback.
He can reach out to support services in case of any issues with the service delivery.
CANCEL:
If Raju cancels the loan pre approval by withdrawing his application, no charges are applied on him. The order was cancelled.
If he cancels, post approval, before disbursement, processing fee was charged.
If he cancels, post approval after disbursement was initiated, processing fee plus penalty was charged.

Flow Diagrams
General Beckn message flow and error handling.

This section is relevant to all the message flows illustrated below and discussed further in the document.

Beckn is a synchronous protocol at its core.

When a network participant(NP1) sends a message to another participant(NP2), the other participant(NP2) immediately returns back an ACK/NACK(Acknowledgement or Negative Acknowledgement in case of error - usually with wrongly formed messages).
An ACK is an indicator that the receiving participant(NP2) will process this message and dispatch an on_xxxxxx message to original NP (NP1)
Subsequently after processing the message NP2 sends back the real response in the corresponding on_xxxxxx message, to which again the first participant(NP1).
This message can contain a message field (for success) or error field (for failure)
NP1 when it receives the on_xxxxxx message, sends back an ACK/NACK (Here in both the cases NP1 will not send any subsequent message).
In the Use case diagrams, this ACK/NACK is not illustrated explicitly to keep the diagrams crisp.
However when writing software we should be prepared to receive these NACK messages as well as error field in the on_xxxxxx messages
While this discussion is from a Beckn perspective, Adapters can provide synchronous modes. For example, the Protocol Server which is the reference implementation of the Beckn Adapter provides a synchronous mode by default. So if your software calls the support endpoint on the BAP Protocol Server, the Protocol Server waits till it gets the on_support and returns back that as the response.



Structure of a message with a NACK

```
{
    "message": {
        "ack": {
            "status": "NACK"
        }
    },
    "error": {
        "code": 400,
        "message": "OpenApiValidator Error at BAP-CLIENT",
    }
}
```

Structure of a on_select message with an error
```
{
    "context": {
        "action": "on_select",
        "version": "1.1.0",
        ...
    },
    "error": {
        "code": 30001,
        "message": "Requested provider is not in the database"
    }
}
```

API Calls and Schema


1.  search
Purpose
This API is used by the BAP to express a farmer’s search intent to discover unsecured credit products from providers (BPPs) on the network. 
Request Payload:
{
    "context": {
        "domain": "credit-services:uki",
        "action": "search",
        "version": "1.1.0",
        "location": {
            "city": {
                "code": "std:95253"
            },
            "country": {
                "code": "IND"
            }
        },
        "bap_id": "krishi-bap.uki.in",
        "bap_uri": "https://krishi-bap.uki.in/protocol",
        "transaction_id": "f75f8973-3261-4931-902f-6a44a7a1ea75",
        "message_id": "2b159ca2-0d68-43f8-a2cd-5e0e2c649ab2",
        "timestamp": "2025-06-02T09:00:00Z",
        "ttl": "PT10S"
    },
    "message": {
        "intent": {
            "descriptor": {
                "name": "Agricultural Input Loan"
            },
            "category": {
                "descriptor": {
                    "code": "unsecured-loan"
                }
            },
            "fulfillment": {
                "type": "digital"
            },
            "item": {
                "tags": [
                    {
                        "descriptor": {
                            "code": "financial-terms"
                        },
                        "list": [
                            {
                                "descriptor": {
                                    "code": "loan-type"
                                },
                                "value": "input-loan"
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "descriptor": {
                            "code": "security-terms"
                        },
                        "list": [
                            {
                                "descriptor": {
                                    "code": "collateral-required"
                                },
                                "value": "yes"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ]
            }
        }
    }
}

